## Example freshclam configuration for Entware ClamAV on legacy QNAP NAS.
##
## Copy this file to the location used by Entware ClamAV (commonly
## /opt/etc/clamav/freshclam.conf or /opt/etc/freshclam.conf) only after
## backing up any existing configuration.
##
## Do not overwrite an existing freshclam.conf without creating a backup first.
##
## Tested with:
##   QNAP TS-469L | QTS 4.3.4 | Entware | ClamAV 1.4.3

## Where Entware ClamAV stores virus definition databases.
DatabaseDirectory /opt/var/lib/clamav

## Owner of the database files after update.
## On the tested TS-469L Entware install, DatabaseOwner admin was required.
## An earlier incorrect setting produced errors involving the "nobody" user.
## Adjust only if your Entware ClamAV package intentionally uses a different user.
DatabaseOwner admin

## Optional: reduce mirror load / noise. Uncomment and tune as needed.
# Checks 12
# MaxAttempts 3
# ConnectTimeout 30
# ReceiveTimeout 60

## Optional: log file. Ensure the directory exists and is writable.
# UpdateLogFile /opt/var/log/freshclam.log
# LogTime yes
# LogVerbose no

## Optional: notify ClamAV daemon after update (only if clamd is running
## from Entware and you intentionally use it). Leave commented for the
## QNAP Antivirus sync workflow.
# NotifyClamd /opt/etc/clamav/clamd.conf
